Hello,

I'd like to make a suggestion for your "LaTeX guides" page (http://www.latex-project.org/guides/) :

"Le Joli Manuel" (in French): it is both an introduction to the general principles (e.g. the separation of the content and the presentation, etc.) and a reference (e.g. list of symbols, font sizes, etc.)

Also the links for "epslatex.pdf" and "short-maths-guide.pdf" seem dead. Maybe the following ones could be used (they are in France, but on the servers of an institution that serves as a CTAN repository, so there are few chances that they become dead)?
http://tex.loria.fr/graph-pack/epslatex.pdf
http://tex.loria.fr/general/downes-short-math-guide.pdf

